# 14. Additional Features Worth Adding

Once the core system is stable, these upgrades would provide substantial operational value.

## A. Purchase and supplier management

Track supplier details, purchase rates, invoices, received quantities, outstanding payments, and material quality.

This would improve the accuracy of production costing.

## B. Automatic production planning

Use:

* Current finished-goods stock.
* Pending orders.
* Average sales.
* Minimum stock levels.
* Raw-material availability.

The ERP could recommend which products to manufacture and how much.

The recommendation should be advisory until an authorized user approves the production plan.

## C. Batch traceability

Every finished packet should be traceable to its production batch.

This would help investigate quality issues, production discrepancies, or customer complaints.

## D. Quality management

Introduce quality checks for:

* Raw materials.
* Dough or prepared mixtures.
* Dried papad.
* Finished packets.
* Packaging integrity.
* Batch approval.

Quality requirements should be configured according to your actual manufacturing procedures.

## E. Low-stock alerts

Notify the Owner when:

* Raw materials fall below minimum stock.
* Packaging materials are insufficient.
* Finished-goods stock is low.
* A salesman needs replenishment.

## F. Automated daily report

At the end of each working day, generate a report containing:

* Sales.
* Collections.
* Expenses.
* Production.
* Packaging.
* Dispatch.
* Stock discrepancies.
* Pending approvals.
* Employee attendance.
* Closing status.

The report should clearly distinguish confirmed figures from incomplete or unavailable data.

## G. Audit and reconciliation centre

Create one screen showing unresolved issues across the ERP.

For example:

| Issue                           | Priority | Recommended action         |
| ------------------------------- | -------- | -------------------------- |
| Google Sheets disconnected      | Critical | Restore persistence        |
| Duplicate employee ID           | Critical | Reconcile identity         |
| Pending batch with stock credit | High     | Investigate ledger         |
| Packaging quantity mismatch     | High     | Reconcile physically       |
| Negative stock                  | High     | Investigate movements      |
| Missing payment record          | High     | Reconcile bill and payment |
| Failed approval execution       | High     | Recover safely             |

This would give you a central place to resolve problems instead of discovering them indirectly.

